ler, creating the political structure later emperors inherited."]],["P",{"class":"reference-highlight"},["svg",{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"30","height":"30","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"2.2","stroke-linecap":"round","stroke-linejoin":"round","class":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},["path",{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"}]],["SPAN",{},"Augustus kept republican forms while holding the powers that made him the dominant ruler."]],["BUTTON",{"aria-busy":"false","class":"reference-primary","disabled":"","type":"button"},"Continue"]],["FIGURE",{"class":"reference-augustus-visual"},["SPAN",{},"Caesar Avgvstvs"],["svg",{"aria-label":"Stylised profile used to represent Augustus","class":"augustus-profile","role":"img","viewBox":"0 0 240 240"},["circle",{"cx":"120","cy":"120","fill":"#eaf7ee","r":"112","stroke":"#0b8f3c","stroke-width":"2"}],["path",{"d":"M71 199c25-31 25-52 10-74-12-17-4-44 18-60 18-14 51-15 69 4 14 15 13 34 3 48-6 8-16 14-27 19 19 13 19 32 10 47-4 7-5 16-2 27l36 17H53z","fill":"#173c25"}]],["OL",{"aria-label":"Augustus timeline"},["LI",{},["SPAN"],"44 BCE"],["LI",{"class":"is-current"},["SPAN"],"27 BCE"],["LI",{},["SPAN"],"14 CE"]],["FIGCAPTION",{"class":"sr-only"},"A stylised profile of Augustus and a timeline from Caesar's death to Augustus's death."]]],["FOOTER",{"class":"reference-footer"},["A",{"class":"reference-footer-link","href":"/courses/roman-empire/lessons/rise-of-the-roman-empire/reference/opening","data-discover":"true"},["svg",{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"18","height":"18","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"2","stroke-linecap":"round","stroke-linejoin":"round","class":"lucide lucide-chevron-left","aria-hidden":"true"},["path",{"d":"m15 18-6-6 6-6"}]],"Back"],["OL",{"aria-label":"Lesson progress","class":"reference-progress-dots"},["LI",{"class":"is-reached"},["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"Step ","1"]],["LI",{"aria-curre